      "patch": "@@ -0,0 +1,3 @@\n+Fixed a use-after-free in :mod:`ssl` when ``SSL_new()`` returns NULL in\n+``newPySSLSocket()``. The error was reported via a dangling pointer after the\n+object had already been freed."
    },
    {
      "sha": "6275d94d644c649b3f536ad40f0c12d89f087e4d",
      "filename": "Modules/_ssl.c",
      "status": "modified",
      "additions": 1,
      "deletions": 1,
      "changes": 2,
      "blob_url": "https://github.com/python/cpython/blob/58390608b2acd53924476d36d683a30c00f41f84/Modules%2F_ssl.c",
      "raw_url": "https://github.com/python/cpython/raw/58390608b2acd53924476d36d683a30c00f41f84/Modules%2F_ssl.c",
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python/cpython/contents/Modules%2F_ssl.c?ref=58390608b2acd53924476d36d683a30c00f41f84",
      "patch": "@@ -844,8 +844,8 @@ newPySSLSocket(PySSLContext *sslctx, PySocketSockObject *sock,\n     self->ssl = SSL_new(ctx);\n     PySSL_END_ALLOW_THREADS\n     if (self->ssl == NULL) {\n+        _setSSLError(get_state_ctx(sslctx), NULL, 0, __FILE__, __LINE__);\n         Py_DECREF(self);\n-        _setSSLError(get_state_ctx(self), NULL, 0, __FILE__, __LINE__);\n         return NULL;\n     }\n     /* bpo43522 and OpenSSL < 1.1.1l: copy hostflags manually */"
    }
